### Metered Geocoding API — via the APISIX gateway (data plane)
###
### Every request below goes through the Apache APISIX proxy ({{gatewayUrl}}),
### NOT directly to the geocoder. APISIX authenticates the caller by API key,
### enforces the tenant's monthly quota, meters the call, then forwards it to the
### geocoder. The JSON responses are identical to the direct service — only the
### entrypoint and the auth/quota behaviour differ.
###
### AUTHENTICATION
###   Send your key in the  X-API-Key  header on EVERY request (all paths are
###   protected, including /health and /features).
###     401  – missing or invalid/deleted key
###     403  – key disabled, or tenant suspended
###     429  – monthly quota exceeded (hard-cap plans only; soft plans bill overage)
###
### GETTING A KEY
###   Sign in to the console (http://localhost:8088) as a tenant user and create
###   a key under "API keys" — the secret is shown once. Paste it into @apiKey.
###   (Disable/enable/delete a key there too; changes take effect within ~1s.)
###
### METERING & BILLING
###   Each served request (2xx) increments your tenant's monthly counter. Live
###   usage shows on the console within a few seconds; rejected calls (401/403/429)
###   are NOT counted. Monthly bills are generated from the recorded usage.
###
### ENDPOINTS (forwarded to the geocoder)
###   GET  /features      – which optional features are enabled
###   GET  /health        – dependency health check (keyed here)
###   GET  /autocomplete  – fast prefix suggestions
###   GET  /geocode       – full-text + vector + geo search (+ interpolation)
###   GET  /address       – structured address search (+ interpolation)
###   GET  /reverse       – reverse geocoding
###   GET  /deep/forward  – deep forward geocoding via Google Maps
###   GET  /deep/reverse  – deep reverse geocoding via Google Maps
###   GET  /deep/nearby   – deep nearby search via Google Places (indexes + returns)
###   GET  /describe      – AI title + description for a place
###   POST /feedback      – popularity feedback loop
###   POST /places        – add a custom place
###   POST /insert        – insert raw OSM element
###   POST /traffic/probe  – submit one GPS ping
###   POST /traffic/probes – submit a GPS trace (batch)
###   GET  /traffic/edge   – live speed for the road edge nearest a point
###   GET  /nearby         – explore nearby places, filter by category/group (metered)
###   GET  /nearby/categories – list filterable groups + values (free: not metered)
###
### ROUTING (proxied through the geocoder → Valhalla internally)
###   GET  /status             – Valhalla engine status
###   POST /route              – turn-by-turn directions (language=ar; ?traffic=true → live-traffic colouring)
###   POST /optimized_route    – reorder stops for shortest tour (TSP)
###   POST /sources_to_targets – time/distance matrix (many → many)
###   POST /isochrone          – reachability polygons
###   POST /locate             – snap coordinates to the road graph
###
### Shared query flags: vector=true|false · ai=true|false · describe=true|false
###
### PERFORMANCE — keep-alive & the X-Cache header
###   • Connection reuse (keep-alive): the server holds connections warm, so a
###     pooled/keep-alive client makes repeat calls ~2 ms round-trips instead of
###     paying a fresh TLS handshake every time. REST-client tools (VS Code /
###     IntelliJ) reuse automatically; programmatic clients should use a session
###     (requests.Session / httpx.Client / a keep-alive agent). With curl, reuse
###     one connection across calls via --next:
###
###       curl -sS -H "X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}" "{{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=cairo&limit=5" \
###         --next -sS -H "X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}" "{{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=cairo&limit=5"
###
###   • /geocode returns an  X-Cache  response header so you can SEE caching:
###       HIT    – served from Redis, Elasticsearch not touched
###       MISS   – computed this time, now cached (next identical call → HIT)
###       BYPASS – not cacheable (describe/ai, or cache disabled)
###     Add  -i  (curl) or check response headers to watch it flip HIT on a repeat.

#@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080
#@apiKey = gk_5c63f22a_rfUC2bRzpUR8GYk1raYsg6fnRjcrmY-J

@gatewayUrl = https://places.nourbyte.com/api
@apiKey = gk_5e464d92_hOKluH0XC-yClI7IO_Yvwc401bNOS4Vm
# Your tenant API key (create one in the console; shown once). Replace this.




# ============================================================================
# AUTH / QUOTA behaviour (try these first to see the gateway in action)
# ============================================================================

### No key → 401 Unauthorized (key-auth rejects before reaching the geocoder)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features

###

### Invalid key → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features
X-API-Key: gk_not_a_real_key

###

### Valid key → 200 (this call is metered against your monthly quota)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /features  –  Feature flags
# ============================================================================

### Report which optional features (vectors, AI) are enabled
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /health  –  Dependency health check (keyed when accessed via the gateway)
# ============================================================================

### ES / PostGIS / NATS / Redis / Ollama status (200 healthy, 503 degraded)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/health
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /autocomplete  –  Fast prefix-based suggestions
#   q (required) · lat/lon (geo-bias) · limit (1–20, default 7)
# ============================================================================

### First few characters
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=metro
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Longer prefix narrows the suggestions
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=cairo
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Arabic prefix
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=5th settlement
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Geo-biased – prefer suggestions near downtown Cairo
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=metro&lat=43.8414059&lon=-79.5109262
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Short prefix with geo-bias, raised limit (nearby restaurants)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=rest&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /geocode  –  Full-text + vector + geo-decay search
#   q (required) · lat/lon (bias) · limit (1–50) · offset · vector · ai
#   describe · effort=high|optimized
#   Response carries a `pagination` block { limit, offset, total, has_more }.
# ============================================================================

### Basic name search
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=9 pentland cres&limit=20
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Geo-biased search near the Giza Pyramids
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=pyramids&lat=29.9792&lon=31.1342&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Multi-word search with Cairo location bias
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Text-only search, vector re-ranking disabled (faster)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandria&limit=10&vector=false
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Fuzzy / typo-tolerant search (Latin typo of an English name)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandira&lat=31.2001&lon=29.9187&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Venue-type search near Cairo
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=restaurant&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=15
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Address-like query: housenumber + street clauses are added automatically
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=10 Tahrir Street, Cairo&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Arabic name search
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=القاهرة&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Include AI descriptions (cached where available, null otherwise)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=cairo tower&lat=30.0459&lon=31.2243&limit=5&describe=true
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Address interpolation – housenumber may be interpolated from neighbours
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=15 Tahrir Street, Cairo&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Paginate – page 1 (check pagination.has_more), then re-request with offset += limit
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram&limit=10&offset=0
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Paginate – page 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram&limit=10&offset=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Effort: optimized – lean fuzzy + rescore over top hits, lighter on ES under load
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10&effort=optimized
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

