# ============================================================================

### Default boost (+1.0)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/feedback?osm_id=n271613766&boost=1.0
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /places  –  Add a custom place (published to NATS, indexed asynchronously)
# ============================================================================

### Minimal – name + coordinates
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/places
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Downtown Cafe",
  "lat": 30.0500,
  "lon": 31.2400,
  "tags": { "amenity": "cafe" }
}

###

### Restaurant with address fields
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/places
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nile View Restaurant",
  "name_en": "Nile View Restaurant",
  "lat": 30.0444,
  "lon": 31.2357,
  "osm_type": "node",
  "admin_level": 8,
  "tags": { "amenity": "restaurant", "cuisine": "egyptian" },
  "addr_housenumber": "5",
  "addr_street": "Corniche El Nil",
  "addr_city": "Cairo",
  "addr_postcode": "11511",
  "addr_country": "EG"
}

###

# ============================================================================
# /insert  –  Raw OSM element insertion (watcher.py message format)
# ============================================================================

### Node with address tags (indexed as an address point)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/insert
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "osm_id": "n999001",
  "osm_type": "node",
  "tags": {
    "name": "Sample Building",
    "building": "yes",
    "addr:housenumber": "42",
    "addr:street": "Tahrir Street",
    "addr:city": "Cairo",
    "addr:postcode": "11511",
    "addr:country": "EG"
  },
  "geom": { "type": "Point", "coordinates": [31.2357, 30.0444] },
  "admin_level": 0,
  "area_km2": 0.0
}

###

# ============================================================================
# LIVE TRAFFIC  –  crowdsourced GPS probes (requires ENABLE_TRAFFIC on geocoder)
#   probe ping: { lat, lon, speed?(m/s), heading?(deg), ts?(epoch seconds) }
# ============================================================================

### Submit a GPS trace (batch map-matches far better than single points)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/traffic/probes
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "device_id": "demo-device-1",
  "points": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 3.0, "ts": 1750000000 },
    { "lat": 30.0429, "lon": 31.2300, "speed": 2.5, "ts": 1750000020 },
    { "lat": 30.0410, "lon": 31.2230, "speed": 3.2, "ts": 1750000045 }
  ]
}

###

### Submit a single GPS ping (device_id is a query param)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/traffic/probe?device_id=demo-device-3
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 4.0, "ts": 1750000000 }

###

### Inspect the current live speed for the edge nearest a point
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/traffic/edge?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /nearby  –  Explore nearby places (filter by category/group)
#   lat/lon (required) · radius m (default 1000, max 50000) · sort=best|distance
#   category=<osm value,…> · group=<food|health|shopping|…> · limit · offset
#   Each result carries category_key/value/group + distance_m. Admin boundaries
#   and area "places" (cities/districts) are excluded — POIs only.
#   Paging: `offset` for shallow pages, or scroll with pagination.next_cursor →
#   pass it back as `cursor` for the next page (no depth limit; offset ignored).
# ============================================================================

### Discovery: filterable groups + their category values. FREE — not metered
### and not counted against quota (still keyed at the gateway).
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby/categories
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### All nearby POIs within 1 km of Tahrir (default sort=best: distance blended
### with importance + popularity). Each result has distance_m. This call is metered.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Nearest-first restaurants + cafes within 800 m (category = precise OSM value;
### comma-separate or repeat the param).
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=800&sort=distance&category=restaurant,cafe
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Coarse group filter: all food places within 1.5 km.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=1500&group=food
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Paginate: page 2 of pharmacies within 5 km (limit/offset like /geocode).
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=5000&category=pharmacy&limit=10&offset=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Scroll page 1: grab pagination.next_cursor from the response…
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=5000&sort=distance&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### …then page 2 via the cursor (offset-free, unbounded depth). Paste the
### next_cursor from the previous response in place of <CURSOR>.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/nearby?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&radius=5000&sort=distance&limit=10&cursor=<CURSOR>
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# ROUTING  –  Valhalla routing engine (geocoder → Valhalla internally)
#   All routing requests are POSTs with a JSON body. Coordinates are {lat, lon}.
#   costing: auto | bicycle | pedestrian | bus | truck | motor_scooter | taxi
#   language: en-US (default) | ar (Arabic narration supported)
#   Wait for GET /status to return 200 before routing (graph build can take
#   several minutes on first start — watch: docker compose logs -f valhalla).
# ============================================================================

### Status – engine version, loaded tileset bbox, available actions
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/status
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Driving directions – Cairo (Tahrir Sq.) → Alexandria, turn-by-turn (English)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers", "language": "en-US" }
}

###

### Driving directions in Arabic – Tahrir → Giza Pyramids
### The geocoder translates Valhalla's en-US output into Arabic instruction templates.
### Street names come from OSM and are already in Arabic script.
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers", "language": "ar" }
}

###

### Multi-stop route – Tahrir → Zamalek → Heliopolis → Giza Pyramids
### "through" points don't split into legs; use "break" to force a leg split
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208, "type": "through" },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201, "type": "through" },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Optimized route (TSP) – Valhalla reorders middle waypoints to minimise drive time
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/optimized_route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Time/distance matrix – one origin (Tahrir) to several destinations at once
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/sources_to_targets
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sources": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 }
  ],
  "targets": [
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "units": "kilometers"
}

###

### Many-to-many matrix – 3 sources × 3 targets = 9 cost cells
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/sources_to_targets
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sources": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 }
  ],
  "targets": [
    { "lat": 30.0479, "lon": 31.2355 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "units": "kilometers"
}

