### Baseline route (no live traffic) – Tahrir → Giza. Note summary.time.
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Live-traffic route – same Tahrir → Giza, opted into current traffic speeds.
### After posting slow /traffic/probes above, summary.time should rise vs. baseline.
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "costing_options": {
    "auto": { "speed_types": ["freeflow", "constrained", "predicted", "current"] }
  },
  "date_time": { "type": 0 },
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Traffic-aware + coloured route – /route with ?traffic=true (no separate endpoint).
### ROUTES USING LIVE TRAFFIC: injects date_time:{type:0} so Valhalla costs edges at
### their live speed from traffic.tar → the ETA (summary.time) and the road choice
### become traffic-aware wherever we have data (edges with none fall back to free-flow).
### Then ANNOTATES: each leg gains a `traffic` array of coloured runs indexing into
### that leg's OWN `shape` (polyline6):
###   { begin_shape_index, end_shape_index, level, live_kph, freeflow_kph, ratio }
###   level = green | yellow | orange | red | unknown; live_kph/ratio = bottleneck edge.
### Plus trip.traffic_coverage = { edges, edges_with_live, coverage_pct, provider_calls }.
### Render: decode legs[].shape and colour each run's [begin..end] slice by level.
###
### COVERAGE is demand-driven & cache-first: for edges with no recent speed in
### Redis, the server fetches them from TomTom on the spot (capped at 15 calls,
### daily-budgeted) and caches them ~10 min (they also flow into traffic.tar, so
### the NEXT route over that corridor is fully traffic-aware). First cold-corridor
### call is slower + spends budget (traffic_coverage.provider_calls > 0); repeats
### are cached (provider_calls: 0). Probes win where present. Egypt + Ontario.
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route?traffic=true
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto"
}

